## pmOS SD userspace-discovery audit

Recorded 2026-09-30T19:40:29.677181+00:00.
Read-only source audit at pocketboot 014a0decdce09eabe88595dffef4bc4b1e4a71b6, following pem120's report
that PocketBoot runs but does not find pmOS on SD. No reporting-unit logs,
card layout, image identity or boot files have been supplied yet. No edits,
new tests/builds or hardware actions were performed for this userspace audit.
The separate SD-host audit is in the evidence note on a7d0397 in this repo.

Confirmed source behavior:
- Discovery accepts removable mmcblk disks (bootflow.rs:377-413,1999-2033).
- Top-level MBR selection accepts primary 0xea entries only, not active 0x83
  (579-620). GPT accepts ESP or XBOOTLDR type GUIDs (998-1003).
- Active 0x83 discovery is only for a nested MBR inside an outer kernel
  partition whose PARTNAME is exactly userdata (652-759), not top-level SD.
- ESP mounts vfat only. XBOOTLDR/nested candidates try ext4/ext2/vfat.
  Mounts are read-only/nosuid/nodev/noexec; ext mounts use noload (1022-1090).
- Scanners accept BLS loader/entries/*.conf or extlinux/extlinux.conf and
  boot/extlinux/extlinux.conf (197-212,1093-1155). Labels such as pmOS_boot
  do not select a boot partition. boot.img and loose kernel files are not
  autodiscovered; staged fastboot Android-image boot is a separate path.
- Config payload paths must exist and remain inside the mounted partition.
  BLS rejects non-ARM64 architecture declarations. Extlinux supports an
  explicit fdt/devicetree, but ignores fdtdir and includes. An entry with a
  whitespace-separated cmdline argument beginning with $ is hidden from
  the menu (bootflow.rs:92-101; main.rs:382-403).
- Discovery runs once after settling (main.rs:171-207). Settle snapshots
  exclude removable disks and can finish after 350ms quiet with internal
  storage present, with a five-second maximum (settle.rs:12-94,378-387).
  Removable block events can reset the quiet timer while settling is active.
  No later hotplug rescan exists: late insertion/enumeration is a distinct
  possible failure, not established as the cause of this report.

Diagnostic caveats:
- fastboot partition getvars filter removable disks; their absence there is
  not proof of kernel invisibility (fastboot/commands/partitions.rs:136-141).
- GPT/MBR rejection details are DEBUG, below this target's INFO log level.
- UMS defaults writable; do not use it to collect this read-only evidence.
- Current pmbootstrap API docs establish separate boot/root and pmOS labels;
  an archived implementation used msdos/ext2/active boot partitions. Neither
  establishes this card's actual/current layout.

Next evidence, before changing code: exact image and installation method;
card present before PocketBoot startup; missing menu entry vs failed launch;
/proc/partitions and MMC/SDHCI/discovery logs from that tablet. If visible,
inspect its partition type/filesystem and BLS/extlinux config/payload paths.
Do not repartition, flip card-detect polarity or add drivers speculatively.
